Sighting quote traces for JA2 Stracciatella (Strategy First SFI-SCLA), ja2-node 2026-10-16. See LICENSE (SFI-SCLA).
In ManSeesMan the merc quotes for first seeing Mike and Joey go through OracleTracedMercDialogue (Oracle.cc, from
0018), which records them as "merc" dialogue events when queued, so the comparers see them like the queued NPC quotes.
No behaviour change. Applied by tools/oracle/build.sh after 0021.

--- a/src/game/Tactical/OppList.cc
+++ b/src/game/Tactical/OppList.cc
@@ -61,6 +61,8 @@
 #include <iterator>
 #include <vector>
 
+BOOLEAN OracleTracedMercDialogue(SOLDIERTYPE const* s, UINT16 quote);
+
 
 static const BOOLEAN gbShowEnemies = FALSE; // XXX seems to be a debug switch
 
@@ -1736,7 +1738,7 @@
 						!(s.usQuoteSaidExtFlags & SOLDIER_QUOTE_SAID_EXT_MIKE))
 					{
 						if (gfMikeShouldSayHi == FALSE) gfMikeShouldSayHi = TRUE;
-						TacticalCharacterDialogue(&s, QUOTE_AIM_SEEN_MIKE);
+						OracleTracedMercDialogue(&s, QUOTE_AIM_SEEN_MIKE);
 						s.usQuoteSaidExtFlags |= SOLDIER_QUOTE_SAID_EXT_MIKE;
 					}
 					break;
@@ -1744,7 +1746,7 @@
 				case JOEY:
 					if (!gfPlayerTeamSawJoey)
 					{
-						TacticalCharacterDialogue(&s, QUOTE_SPOTTED_JOEY);
